## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end data sharing, isolation, masking, and real-time updates in Snowflake core.

## Key Concepts
- Secure Data Shares, ROW ACCESS POLICIES, Dynamic Masking
- Streams/Tasks or Snowpipe for near-real-time updates
- Per-tenant data modeling and governance

## Code Example
```sql
-- provider side
CREATE SHARE provider_share;
CREATE SECURE VIEW curated.tenant_view AS SELECT * FROM curated.ALL_DATA WHERE TENANT_ID = CURRENT_TENANT();
GRANT USAGE ON DATABASE curated TO consumer_account;
GRANT SELECT ON VIEW curated.tenant_view TO consumer_account;
-- masking policy example
CREATE MASKING POLICY pii_mask AS RETURN NULL ON (CURRENT_ROLE() != 'DATA_CONSUMER');
ALTER VIEW curated.tenant_view MODIFY SET MASKING POLICY pii_mask;
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you audit cross-tenant data access?
- How would you handle schema evolution in the shared data product?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end Snowflake-core pipeline design: ingestion, streams, tasks, late data handling, and anomaly scoring across accounts.

## Key Concepts
- Snowflake Streams, Tasks, external stages, MERGE, watermarking, rolling baselines, alerting.
- Data governance: access control, masking, retention.

## Code Example
```sql
-- Core objects (illustrative)
CREATE OR REPLACE STAGE RAW_EVENTS_STAGE URL='s3://region-lake/raw' FILE_FORMAT=(TYPE='JSON');
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE RAW_EVENTS(
  event_id STRING, customer_id STRING, region STRING, amount NUMBER, ts TIMESTAMP_NTZ
);
CREATE OR REPLACE STREAM RAW_EVENTS_STREAM ON TABLE RAW_EVENTS (APPEND_ONLY = FALSE);
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE FRAUD_SCORES(customer_id STRING, region STRING, date DATE, score FLOAT);
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE FRAUD_WATERMARK(date DATE, max_ts TIMESTAMP_NTZ);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test late-arrival handling and boundary conditions?
- How would you scale the rolling baseline computation to thousands of regions and customers?
